        "description": "<p>Start with the ingredients you use most: fresh pepper, real cardamom, warming cloves, raw honey, and everyday kitchen staples from Kerala.</p><p>Many grow in misty hill regions where slower cycles help hold aroma and natural oils. The difference shows up as soon as the spice hits heat.</p><p>Cardamom and black pepper are the big two Kerala spices. Idukki grows most of Kerala's cardamom, and pepper vines climb the same shade trees on many hill farms. Cloves from Adimali round out the three spices that lose their aroma fastest once ground, which is why they are the best to buy whole from the farm first. New to Kerala spices? Our <a href=\"/blogs/cooking-spices/kerala-spices-list\">list of Kerala spices</a> explains what each one is for, and our <a href=\"/blogs/cooking-spices/spice-names-malayalam-english\">spice names in Malayalam and English</a> helps if a recipe uses local words. Not sure what to pick? Message us on WhatsApp at +91 88482 65849 and tell us what you cook.</p>",
